-- The judge or justice (in the court of subsection (5)) who is satisfied that the periods of detention have expired and proceedings have not been instituted, or that the continued detention will not be required,
-- "shall" order the thing returned (c) to the person from whom it was seized if their possession is lawful; (d) to the lawful owner if their possession is unlawful and the owner is known. A thing seized when it was
-- not in the possession of any person, with an owner known, is reached by neither paragraph (fork F9): NOTHING.
GIVEN `the judge or justice is satisfied that the periods of detention provided for or ordered under subsections (1) to (3) have expired and proceedings have not been instituted in which the thing detained may be required, or that the continued detention of the thing seized will not be required for any purpose mentioned in subsection (1) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `possession of the thing by the person from whom it was seized is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `possession of the thing by the person from whom it was seized is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing was seized when it was not in the possession of any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490(9) order`
`s 490(9) the order the judge or justice shall make` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judge or justice is satisfied that the periods of detention provided for or ordered under subsections (1) to (3) have expired and proceedings have not been instituted in which the thing detained may be required, or that the continued detention of the thing seized will not be required for any purpose mentioned in subsection (1) or (4)` THEN JUST `s 490(9) paragraphs (c) and (d) require no order`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is satisfied that the periods of detention provided for or ordered under subsections (1) to (3) in respect of anything seized have expired"
        IF `possession of the thing by the person from whom it was seized is lawful` THEN JUST `s 490(9)(c) order the thing returned to the person from whom it was seized`
        IF `possession of the thing by the person from whom it was seized is unlawful` AND `the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is known` THEN JUST `s 490(9)(d) order the thing returned to the lawful owner or the person lawfully entitled to its possession`
        IF `possession of the thing by the person from whom it was seized is unlawful` THEN JUST `s 490(9) paragraphs (c) and (d) require no order`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) if possession of it by the person from whom it was seized is unlawful and the lawful owner or person who is lawfully entitled to its possession is known"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)

